1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:18,600
Flamme.

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,930
You mean "Master."

5
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:22,890
What is it?

6
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,850
Do you really think it's unfair?

7
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:32,740
Frieren, do you remember Basalt's last words?

8
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,650
No.

9
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:39,450
Their kind uses words only to deceive humans.

10
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:41,200
That's right.

11
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:44,500
They're nothing more than monsters
capable of speech.

12
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:48,830
That's the true nature of the
creatures I call demons.

13
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:55,970
They don't play fair,
so we must be even more unfair.

14
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:03,020
If it allows me to exterminate demonkind,
then I will gladly embrace this dishonor.

15
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:10,020
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

16
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:12,440
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

17
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:15,360
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

18
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:16,990
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

19
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:19,320
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

20
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:21,660
<i>Across this land</i>

21
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:23,990
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

22
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:26,460
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

23
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:38,760
<i>The story ends</i>

24
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:41,260
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

25
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:44,100
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

26
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:45,770
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

27
00:01:45,770 --> 00:01:48,270
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

28
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:50,440
<i>Makes people forget</i>

29
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:53,230
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

30
00:01:53,230 --> 00:01:55,030
<i>Begin to rust</i>

31
00:01:55,030 --> 00:01:56,860
<i>Just the same</i>

32
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:59,160
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

33
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,490
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

34
00:02:02,490 --> 00:02:04,370
<i>And they live on</i>

35
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,910
<i>We chose the same path</i>

36
00:02:06,910 --> 00:02:09,040
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

37
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:10,580
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

38
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:14,840
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

39
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,210
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

40
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:17,300
<i>Even now</i>

41
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:19,680
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

42
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:23,220
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

43
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:24,890
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

44
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:46,790
<i>The bleeding won't stop.</i>

45
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:48,910
<i>This is the end.</i>

46
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:52,120
Your plan has failed.

47
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,090
You're right.

48
00:02:55,090 --> 00:02:57,880
But Frieren won't escape unscathed.

49
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:02,260
She must be fighting Lady Aura by now.

50
00:03:02,970 --> 00:03:07,140
Previously, we were forced to
retreat by the party of heroes.

51
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:10,980
But this time, there are
no heroes to protect her.

52
00:03:12,230 --> 00:03:15,230
It's true that Frieren is a threat to us,

53
00:03:15,230 --> 00:03:18,900
but she has far less mana than Lady Aura.

54
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:23,740
If she engages her directly,
Frieren will lose.

55
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:26,740
Then Frieren will win.

56
00:03:27,950 --> 00:03:32,410
She'd never directly engage a demon.

57
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:35,080
I know she'll trick Aura and kill her.

58
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:38,090
<i>Nonsense.</i>

59
00:03:38,090 --> 00:03:43,930
<i>Frieren the Slayer has always
engaged us directly.</i>

60
00:03:45,510 --> 00:03:48,310
<i>Why do I feel like something is wrong?</i>

61
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:51,980
<i>This girl's mana is weak,</i>

62
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:56,860
<i>and yet I was overwhelmed by the
sheer number of her rapid attacks.</i>

63
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:02,570
<i>But how was she able to do that
without exhausting her mana?</i>

64
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:08,080
I understand now. Is that even possible?

65
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:11,330
So Frieren does the same.

66
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:13,830
What you've done isn't fair.

67
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:18,670
You're a disgrace to all mages.

68
00:04:18,670 --> 00:04:22,300
Ms. Frieren knows that better than anyone.

69
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:34,270
What a dreadful sight.

70
00:04:35,730 --> 00:04:37,440
Looks like an elf village.

71
00:04:49,530 --> 00:04:51,540
Basalt the Throne,

72
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:53,830
a general of the Demon King's army.

73
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:58,210
He must've led his forces here
to destroy this village.

74
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:04,340
Are you the one who killed him?
You seem nearly dead yourself.

75
00:05:10,930 --> 00:05:13,020
That's a lot of mana.

76
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:14,480
You must be powerful.

77
00:05:14,770 --> 00:05:17,390
Did you engage the demons directly?

78
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:22,980
What a fool you are.

79
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:26,570
Why do people always engage
their enemies directly?

80
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:29,110
Run, hide, take your enemies by surprise...

81
00:05:29,110 --> 00:05:31,740
There are plenty of other options.

82
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:35,330
I'll never understand strong mages.

83
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,500
But you do.

84
00:05:38,330 --> 00:05:39,250
What?

85
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:42,880
You should understand how I feel...

86
00:05:45,050 --> 00:05:49,970
because you're a far more powerful mage.

87
00:06:00,270 --> 00:06:02,270
What makes you say that?

88
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:05,280
Just a feeling.

89
00:06:07,150 --> 00:06:09,410
What's your name?

90
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,870
What happened to the village?

91
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:19,710
Its people are dead, down to
the last woman and child.

92
00:06:20,870 --> 00:06:25,250
I was the strongest, but I still
couldn't protect them.

93
00:06:25,750 --> 00:06:27,920
You really are a fool.

94
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:31,300
If I'd been in your shoes,
I wouldn't have hesitated to run.

95
00:06:32,550 --> 00:06:33,850
Put me down.

96
00:06:33,850 --> 00:06:35,310
No.

97
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:38,850
You have potential.
You're going to be my apprentice.

98
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:45,730
And you know you wouldn't have survived
if I hadn't happened upon you.

99
00:06:45,730 --> 00:06:50,070
On top of failing to protect the village,
you nearly died yourself.

100
00:06:50,570 --> 00:06:52,660
Your death truly would've been in vain.

101
00:06:55,450 --> 00:06:56,660
We're being pursued.

102
00:06:57,700 --> 00:07:00,540
They're stronger than the general you killed.

103
00:07:07,710 --> 00:07:09,970
Interesting creatures, aren't they?

104
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:13,010
They had every intention
of catching us off guard

105
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:15,470
by concealing their mana
until just before they struck,

106
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:20,850
but the moment they realized we were mages,
they stepped out into the open.

107
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:24,610
They're cunning and they don't play fair,

108
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:29,320
but every last one of them has a ridiculous
sense of pride when it comes to magic.

109
00:07:30,150 --> 00:07:34,910
Human mage, leave the elf girl and go.

110
00:07:35,370 --> 00:07:38,040
Will you let me go if I do?

111
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:40,700
"Kill all the elves."

112
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:43,040
Those were the Demon King's orders.

113
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,960
Your life matters not to me.

114
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:47,750
I see.

115
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:58,180
Frieren, it's true that I'm painfully aware
of what it's like to be a powerful mage.

116
00:07:58,930 --> 00:08:02,310
I know exactly how these creatures feel, too.

117
00:08:02,810 --> 00:08:08,190
I know the absolute confidence they
have in the magics they've studied.

118
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:12,690
In other words, they're stupidly
proud and overconfident.

119
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:32,510
Frieren, unlike you,
they judged me a weakling.

120
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:40,180
Though they were exceptional mages,
their overconfidence cost them their lives.

121
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:45,230
You hid your strength by controlling
how much mana you release.

122
00:08:46,650 --> 00:08:47,560
That's right.

123
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:52,360
Deceive and kill your enemies by allowing
them to miscalculate your strength.

124
00:08:53,070 --> 00:08:58,490
It's a cowardly and unfair way to fight
that makes a mockery of magic.

125
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:16,630
Your injuries are looking a lot better.

126
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:21,760
Shall we begin your training?

127
00:09:23,270 --> 00:09:24,520
Flamme.

128
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,020
You mean "Master."

129
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:33,480
Demons took everything from me.

130
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:34,690
Me, too.

131
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:38,780
I hate them so much that I wish
I could exterminate every last one.

132
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:40,030
Me, too.

133
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,910
But I love magic.

134
00:09:43,910 --> 00:09:45,160
So do I.

135
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:52,920
Which is why only you and I should become
cowards who make a mockery of magic.

136
00:09:55,130 --> 00:09:58,010
What should I do to train?

137
00:09:58,010 --> 00:10:02,550
Try limiting the mana you release
to one-tenth of its normal volume.

138
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:07,810
Impressive. You're controlling it well.

139
00:10:08,850 --> 00:10:11,980
Any elf can do this.

140
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:17,110
While you do that, we'll work on your
fundamentals and raise your base mana level.

141
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:19,150
That's all?

142
00:10:19,150 --> 00:10:20,410
Simple, right?

143
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:26,540
By the way, how long should
I keep suppressing my mana?

144
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:29,210
It starts to get tiring
if I do it for too long.

145
00:10:29,210 --> 00:10:31,040
As long as I do.

146
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,460
For life.

147
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:37,340
You'll spend your entire life fooling demons.

148
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,640
Lügner is dead.

149
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:48,140
Now all your executioners
have been eliminated.

150
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:50,270
You've failed, Aura.

151
00:10:50,890 --> 00:10:53,230
You're right. It's a shame.

152
00:10:53,650 --> 00:10:57,900
But if I can defeat you here,
then it won't have been for nothing.

153
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:05,990
In this battle, you've released numerous
immortal soldiers from my control.

154
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:12,000
Was it wise to expend so much mana against me?

155
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:16,210
<i>The Scales of Obedience.</i>

156
00:11:16,670 --> 00:11:19,340
<i>When two souls are placed on the scale,</i>

157
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:22,760
<i>whichever has more mana
forces the other to submit.</i>

158
00:11:23,590 --> 00:11:29,060
<i>Aura can only use such a risky spell
because of her tremendous amount of mana.</i>

159
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,350
<i>Generally speaking,</i>

160
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:34,520
<i>a person's mana increases in proportion
with the time spent training.</i>

161
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:39,360
<i>I can feel it in the mana pouring off Aura.</i>

162
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:43,530
<i>She's a great demon who has lived
for over five hundred years,</i>

163
00:11:43,530 --> 00:11:47,030
<i>and she's spent most of her life training.</i>

164
00:11:48,370 --> 00:11:49,870
<i>Five hundred years, huh?</i>

165
00:11:50,370 --> 00:11:53,170
<i>That's fairly long-lived for a demon.</i>

166
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:55,380
<i>I doubt she's been challenged before.</i>

167
00:11:56,380 --> 00:12:00,550
<i>I can learn so much just from
the mana flowing off her.</i>

168
00:12:01,050 --> 00:12:05,930
<i>Regardless, demons don't conceal
their mana—nor can they.</i>

169
00:12:06,970 --> 00:12:08,140
A pity.

170
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:13,560
Auserlese.

171
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,570
Master.

172
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:22,570
Demons are cunning, aren't they?

173
00:12:22,570 --> 00:12:26,700
Why don't they constantly suppress
their mana like you do?

174
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:29,450
They can't.

175
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:33,460
Demons are individualists,

176
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:37,960
but they form the barest connections
needed to fight against humankind.

177
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:41,840
What do you think an organization
needs to function?

178
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,550
Order?

179
00:12:44,550 --> 00:12:45,470
That's right.

180
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:49,970
In other words, you need someone
important to lead an organization.

181
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:52,430
In the case of humans,

182
00:12:52,430 --> 00:12:57,480
importance is determined by status
and wealth, like they do in this nation.

183
00:12:58,190 --> 00:13:02,230
That well-dressed man exiting
that palace is a man of importance.

184
00:13:03,150 --> 00:13:05,360
It's hard to tell which humans are important,

185
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:09,450
so they dress themselves up
to make it obvious.

186
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:11,620
Demons are different?

187
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:16,540
They haven't changed a bit
since they were monsters.

188
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:18,540
Might makes right.

189
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:20,750
It's far easier to understand than humans.

190
00:13:21,210 --> 00:13:23,260
You can tell who's strong
just by looking at them.

191
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:25,010
You mean mana.

192
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:30,050
Mana is to them what status
and wealth are for humans.

193
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:32,510
It's dignity itself.

194
00:13:33,010 --> 00:13:38,190
They may temporarily suppress
their mana for the sake of stealth,

195
00:13:38,190 --> 00:13:42,650
but none are foolish enough
to suppress their mana all the time.

196
00:13:42,650 --> 00:13:47,070
It's the difference between a noble
sneaking out into town incognito

197
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:51,410
and that same noble debasing themselves by
abandoning their status and wealth entirely.

198
00:13:52,450 --> 00:13:55,200
The world of demons is cruel.

199
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:59,330
They'd never grant any dignity
to those with little mana.

200
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:04,670
So the stronger they are, the more desperate
they are to show off their mana.

201
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:10,180
For them, there's no benefit to
constantly suppressing their mana.

202
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:12,930
It doesn't even occur to them to do it.

203
00:14:13,510 --> 00:14:15,140
It's a pity, isn't it?

204
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:20,690
Just as humans are bound by status
and wealth, demons are bound by mana.

205
00:14:20,690 --> 00:14:25,480
Despite their pride in
and unparalleled love for magic,

206
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:28,320
they can't control their own mana.

207
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:32,910
Frieren, you're lucky you're not a demon.

208
00:14:32,910 --> 00:14:36,200
You're right. I wouldn't be able
to deceive them if I were.

209
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:44,090
It's been three years since you
started suppressing your mana.

210
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:47,460
Looks like I was right about you.

211
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:54,600
You've grown much better at that.

212
00:14:56,930 --> 00:15:00,020
Frieren, do you still love magic?

213
00:15:01,350 --> 00:15:03,560
Where did that come from, Master?

214
00:15:04,810 --> 00:15:06,230
Somewhat, I suppose.

215
00:15:07,110 --> 00:15:11,910
Long ago, you once confidently
answered that you loved magic.

216
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,410
That was only fifty years ago.

217
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:17,160
You're right.

218
00:15:18,910 --> 00:15:24,170
In the end, all I could do
was teach you to fight.

219
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:26,420
Magic for revenge.

220
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,130
Do you regret it?

221
00:15:29,710 --> 00:15:35,010
No. I'm glad I taught my magic to you.

222
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:37,970
Given how long you'll live,

223
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:42,060
you might eventually become strong
enough to defeat the Demon King.

224
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:47,360
Frieren, I have one request.

225
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:48,900
What is it?

226
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:53,320
Plant flowers around my grave.

227
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:55,030
That doesn't seem like you.

228
00:15:55,030 --> 00:15:56,200
I know.

229
00:15:57,780 --> 00:16:05,040
Frieren, my favorite spell
creates a field of beautiful flowers.

230
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:09,460
My parents taught it to me when I was little.

231
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:12,130
It's what made me love magic.

232
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:13,930
Huh.

233
00:16:16,050 --> 00:16:18,180
Teach me that spell.

234
00:16:26,310 --> 00:16:27,900
Listen to me, Frieren.

235
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:31,440
You must never seek to leave
your name in history.

236
00:16:31,990 --> 00:16:33,820
Live in obscurity.

237
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:39,780
You won't leave your name in history
until you defeat the Demon King.

238
00:17:39,510 --> 00:17:43,720
I've heard there's a long-lived
mage in these woods.

239
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:45,600
Are you her?

240
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:50,610
I've lived a long time, but I haven't
done much with my life.

241
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,730
I'm not exceptional.

242
00:17:53,730 --> 00:17:57,240
Huh. What do you think, Heiter?

243
00:17:58,910 --> 00:18:01,870
She has roughly one-fifth of my mana.

244
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:04,240
It's not bad.

245
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:06,120
Who's this irritating guy?

246
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:10,580
Leave. You don't have business
with a mediocre mage, do you?

247
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:15,260
No, you're stronger than
any mage I've ever met.

248
00:18:16,510 --> 00:18:18,260
What makes you say that?

249
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,930
Just a feeling.

250
00:18:26,350 --> 00:18:27,480
Auserlese.

251
00:18:46,870 --> 00:18:48,870
You seem happy, Aura.

252
00:18:48,870 --> 00:18:51,120
Are you certain you'll win?

253
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,130
You'll see.

254
00:18:55,170 --> 00:18:56,880
<i>Frieren the Slayer.</i>

255
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:01,840
<i>You made your first major
appearance eighty years ago.</i>

256
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:05,640
<i>With the party of heroes,
you defeated the Demon King.</i>

257
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:09,350
<i>You're a mysterious elven mage
whose age is unknown.</i>

258
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:15,480
<i>But it doesn't matter how
long-lived a mage you are.</i>

259
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:18,360
<i>Your mana tells me everything
I need to know.</i>

260
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:21,820
<i>I can see it quite clearly.</i>

261
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:27,450
<i>You're an exceptional mage,
but your mana itself is unimpressive.</i>

262
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:32,170
<i>You can't have had more than a
hundred years or so of training.</i>

263
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:35,590
<i>Not only that, but you've barely
changed since eighty years ago.</i>

264
00:19:36,090 --> 00:19:39,300
<i>Were you honing other skills
instead of working on your mana?</i>

265
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:42,090
<i>Or were you simply wasting your life away?</i>

266
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:47,600
<i>Either way, you are no match for me.</i>

267
00:19:57,150 --> 00:19:58,860
I win.

268
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:06,370
All that's left is to sever your head myself.

269
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:14,710
<i>It wasn't even necessary
to exhaust Frieren's mana.</i>

270
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:17,380
<i>I needn't have been so cautious.</i>

271
00:20:18,290 --> 00:20:21,010
<i>She defeated many of my
immortal soldiers, too.</i>

272
00:20:21,010 --> 00:20:22,760
<i>I'll have to replenish their numbers later.</i>

273
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,260
<i>What's this?</i>

274
00:20:28,390 --> 00:20:31,430
<i>The scales are starting to tip toward Frieren.</i>

275
00:20:32,020 --> 00:20:35,650
You placed my soul on the scales, Aura.

276
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:41,480
Honestly, I would've been in trouble
if you'd tried to overwhelm me with numbers.

277
00:20:41,940 --> 00:20:45,410
I'm glad you're so confident in your own mana.

278
00:20:46,110 --> 00:20:48,120
Now I can finally defeat you.

279
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:50,540
What do you mean?

280
00:20:50,990 --> 00:20:53,040
You should've figured it out by now.

281
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:56,040
I've been suppressing my mana.

282
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:59,540
You misjudged the situation, Aura.

283
00:21:01,250 --> 00:21:06,180
That's impossible. That wouldn't
have escaped my notice.

284
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:10,760
There was no hint of the instability
or variation in mana output

285
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:12,310
that comes with suppression.

286
00:21:12,810 --> 00:21:17,980
I'm surprised. Demons are capable
of observing mana that precisely?

287
00:21:18,650 --> 00:21:21,570
Sounds like my master made the
right call with her methods.

288
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:27,200
I've spent most of my life
suppressing my mana.

289
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:29,410
This state has become natural for me.

290
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:35,080
Are you stupid? Why would you
do something so pointless?

291
00:21:35,290 --> 00:21:37,960
You're right. It's stupid.

292
00:21:38,670 --> 00:21:40,710
But it lets me beat your kind.

293
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:45,970
This is absurd.

294
00:21:46,380 --> 00:21:49,220
I'm a great demon who's lived
for over five hundred years.

295
00:21:51,180 --> 00:21:54,390
Aura, the person standing before you...

296
00:21:57,520 --> 00:22:00,650
is a mage who's lived
for over a thousand years.

297
00:22:14,330 --> 00:22:15,540
<i>Frieren.</i>

298
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:19,290
<i>Just as demons deceive humankind with words,</i>

299
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,040
<i>you must use your mana to deceive demons.</i>

300
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:25,050
Aura,

301
00:22:26,090 --> 00:22:27,300
kill yourself.

302
00:22:36,180 --> 00:22:37,770
Impossible.

303
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:41,400
H-How could I...?

304
00:22:50,070 --> 00:22:52,620
<i>And you alright</i>

305
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,120
<i>Can you hear me</i>

306
00:22:55,910 --> 00:23:02,000
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

307
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,340
<i>Crying excessively</i>

308
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:07,510
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

309
00:23:07,510 --> 00:23:13,550
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

310
00:23:13,550 --> 00:23:17,270
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

311
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:20,020
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

312
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:25,690
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

313
00:23:25,690 --> 00:23:29,240
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

314
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:32,280
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

315
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:37,030
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

316
00:23:37,030 --> 00:23:43,120
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

317
00:23:43,120 --> 00:23:48,960
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

318
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:54,970
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

319
00:23:54,970 --> 00:24:00,730
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

320
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:03,690
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

321
00:24:03,690 --> 00:24:06,610
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

322
00:24:06,610 --> 00:24:12,780
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

323
00:24:12,780 --> 00:24:15,450
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

324
00:24:15,450 --> 00:24:19,370
<i>for you to come back home</i>

325
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:22,910
Do you have someone to praise you?

326
00:24:20,750 --> 00:24:22,910
You're traveling to heaven, then?

327
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:23,080
I'm not sure I understand...

328
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:24,710
You've got a nice body, old man.

329
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:26,210
The largest magical city in the
northern lands, Äußerst.

330
00:24:24,420 --> 00:24:26,040
What's a first-class mage?

331
00:24:25,080 --> 00:24:27,170
What is that trinket?

332
00:24:26,040 --> 00:24:27,920
It means we're elves.

333
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:30,090
It's the winters of the northern lands.
